# Flutter/Dart/Pub related
**/doc/api/
**/ios/Flutter/.last_build_id
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.pub-cache/
.pub/
/build/

# Gradle writes here too, and the root-only rule above never covered it. A
# problems-report.html had been committed and was then copied into the PUBLIC
# export, because that export walks `git ls-files`.
android/build/
**/.gradle/
/coverage/

# Symbolication related
app.*.symbols

# Obfuscation related
app.*.map.json

# Android Studio will place build artifacts here
/android/app/debug
/android/app/profile
/android/app/release

# Prevent real Google/Firebase configs from leaking (was a typo: "google-service"
# singular never matched the real "google-services.json" → the file stayed tracked).
google-services.json
app/google-services.json
android/app/google-services.json

# wrangler files
.wrangler
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example
!.env.example

# Source images for the cover library. Converted into covers/ as 800x800 webp
# by tool/ scripts; the originals are 356MB of jpg/png and must never be
# committed — a single "git add ." would put them in history permanently.
new_covers/

# ── WORKING NOTES, NOT PART OF THE APP ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# Development journals and internal review notes: operational detail,
# environment specifics, device logs and unfixed weaknesses. None of it is
# source and none of it belongs in a PUBLISHED tree.
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PRIVATE AND STAYS PRIVATE. The public release is a
# separate repo produced by tool/export_public_source.ps1, exported
# history-free — so "not in the public tree" and "not tracked here" were never
# actually the same requirement. session_progress.md is tracked from
# 2026-09-01 because a development journal is worth having in history when the
# history is private.
#
# WHAT KEEPS IT OUT OF THE PUBLIC REPO IS THE EXPORT SCRIPT, NOT THIS FILE.
# The export copies every path `git ls-files` returns, so tracking it here is
# exactly what would publish it. That script's $excludeExact has named it since
# before it was tracked — it was written as belt-and-braces and is now the only
# thing preventing it — and a post-export check refuses to publish if it
# reaches the output tree by any route. Do not remove either.
#
# AUVY_AUDIT.md stays untracked: it is a point-in-time review of weaknesses
# rather than a running record, and it has no value in history.
AUVY_AUDIT.md
